# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# There was no .dockerignore until 15 Aug 2026, so every `docker-compose
# build` shipped the ENTIRE tree to the daemon — node_modules, git history,
# dists, and (once the model-derivation spike landed) 3.0 GB of GGUF
# weights. Measured: the context passed 1.2 GB and was still climbing when
# the build was killed. The Dockerfiles copy what they need; nothing here
# is load-bearing for an image.
#
# Rule of thumb for additions: if a service does not COPY it, it does not
# belong in the context.

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.build
**/.build

# Model weights and experiment data (gigabytes; never in an image)
**/data/*.gguf
experiments/*/data
models/data

# VCS and local tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
**/.DS_Store
*.log
**/*.log

# Local state, secrets, identities — must never reach an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.identity
.mcp.json
.ec2-last-sync

# Docs and notes: not needed to run a service
docs
**/*.md
!README.md

# Test and scratch artifacts
coverage
**/coverage
tmp
**/tmp

# The ephemeral packaging is not part of any container image. It carries its
# own node_modules, its own vendored libraries and the bundled services — about
# 250 MB that the daemon has no use for. Added 16 Aug after the context reached
# 672 MB and the identity build was still uploading.
imagine/
build/
